cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StericRender in your research, please cite the software and the underlying methods listed in the README."
title: "StericRender: Topographic Steric Mapping with Molecular Visualisation"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James
    family-names: "O'Brien"
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, The University of Manchester"
version: "1.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21474975"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JamesOBrien2/StericRender"
url: "https://github.com/JamesOBrien2/StericRender"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - buried volume
  - molecular visualisation
  - steric maps
  - organometallic chemistry
abstract: >-
  StericRender computes topographic steric maps and buried volume (%VBur)
  descriptors for molecular structures and produces publication-quality SVG
  figures from the command line.
